WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.863
Eyes on the road, or on the clock. Wattzup tells you what's coming.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.824
The interval card names the segment: work, round five of eight, thirty-two seconds

00:00:12.824 --> 00:00:13.418
left.

00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:17.502
Below it, what's next: recover, twenty seconds at level six.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.284
Beeps start off. Tap the bell, and a tone confirms it: you'll hear each change

00:00:24.284 --> 00:00:24.969
coming.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.537
In the last three seconds, the time turns volt, and three short beeps count you

00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:35.124
down.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.368
Then the banner: Recover, level six, twenty seconds, then work at eighteen.

00:00:42.568 --> 00:00:44.342
A screen reader hears it too.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.156
Back to work: Work, eighteen, go!

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.958
And on the cool-down, the card reads Last stretch.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.269
On a phone, the banner sits right on top of the numbers.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.548
What the tests prove: each change has its own tone, higher for work, lower for

00:01:20.548 --> 00:01:21.314
recover.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.390
And a paused countdown neither pulses nor beeps.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.506
That is journey eight. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:32.506 --> 00:01:33.801
training display.
